{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You shall not take [a wife] to rival.</b> He stated this because without it, he would not have forbidden a wife's sister, since she is not the wife's close kin and the wife herself is permitted. But He forbade her so that they not become rivals. Therefore He forbade her only during her sister's lifetime — and so it is not with all other forbidden relations."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:44.872275240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}